      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Nasopharyngeal carcinoma is a tumor that is uncommon in children and adolescents. Presenting symptoms may be subtle and may include epistaxis, neck pain, hearing impairment, otorrhea, rhinorrhea, and, most likely, painless cervical adenopathy. The tumor is curable, but late diagnosis makes this possibility much less likely. Diagnosis of this tumor requires a high index of suspicion on the part of clinicians treating the pediatric population."},
